+ *
+ * The AP can hang on a spontaneous fatal-triggered SSR. The console always ends
+ * on "port failed halt", and the next print normally follows 43-47 ms later, so
+ * the hang is bounded by two adjacent printk calls and its site is enumerable
+ * from source. This traces each step of that window so a hang names its own
+ * step: the LAST "q6v5-trace:" line printed is the call that never returned.
+ *
+ * One print per step, placed immediately BEFORE the call. The next step's print
+ * is itself proof the previous call returned, which halves the print volume --
+ * and print volume matters here, because the console is a 115200 baud serial
+ * line where a 40-character line costs ~3.5 ms of the 43-47 ms window.
+ *
+ * Remove this whole block once the hang site is known.
+ */
